    <string name="settings_search_api">Use the DeepSeek Search API for web search</string>
    <string name="settings_search_api_on">On: you can see the queries and results; billed per search (¥5 per 1,000), needs a DeepSeek key</string>
    <string name="settings_search_api_off_no_search">Off: \"%1$s\" has no server-side search, so there is no web search</string>
    <string name="settings_search_api_off">Off: uses the server-side search built into \"%1$s\"; you can\'t see what it searched</string>
    <string name="settings_fetch_fallback">Use DeepSeek Fetch when a page won\'t open</string>
    <string name="settings_fetch_fallback_no_key">On, but there\'s no DeepSeek key, so it has no effect yet</string>
    <string name="settings_fetch_fallback_on">On: when a site blocks the device\'s request or won\'t open, the Fetch API reads it instead (¥0.005 each, spent only when blocked); the main agent and subagents both use it, and with server-side search the main agent can open pages too</string>
    <string name="settings_fetch_fallback_off">Off: a page that won\'t open stays unopened; with server-side search the main agent can\'t open pages</string>
